        "original_id": "66957c38-2f16-58b4-8b9c-5b38d449611f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Yuh-Line Niou, Sheldon Silver, Alice Cancel\n- Organizations: Democratic Party, New York State Assembly\n- Roles: Member of the New York State Assembly, Speaker of the New York State Assembly\n- Places: New York City, New York\n\nFacts:\n- Sheldon Silver was born on February 13, 1944.\n- In 1994, Sheldon Silver became Speaker of the New York State Assembly.\n- In 2015, Sheldon Silver's tenure as Speaker of the New York State Assembly ended after his arrest on federal corruption charges.\n- In 2016, Alice Cancel was defeated in the Democratic primary for her Assembly seat by Yuh-Line Niou.\n- Yuh-Line Niou is a Democratic Party member of the New York State Assembly for New York's 65th district.\n- The New York State Assembly seat for the 65th district held by Yuh-Line Niou was previously held by Sheldon Silver.",
